{"title":"Mock AIME II 2012 Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem:\">Problem:</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_II_2012_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem:\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/9/2e978a0825dc57184086cbb00ed2da1875cf3a9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n=\\sum_{i=0}^{n}f(i)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"101\" height=\"48\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/3/9238d82d59d5dfe79e96d916bfdf2f4acc4ed3be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abb88988bde58a51f19f59c763ee7e64b140e96d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" />.  Given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is a polynomial, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/1/8b19d463d56a72694a86ad5305d8888fd255b8ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, a_2+1, a_3+8, a_4+27, a_5+64, a_6+125, \\cdots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"363\" height=\"16\" /> is an arithmetic sequence, find the smallest positive integer value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/1/191d57d1e5f185fb30c1bc518df495e0b7d7bbf2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)&lt;-2012$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"109\" height=\"18\" />.  \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_II_2012_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><b>Lemma:</b>  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is a quadratic\n</p><p><br />\n<b>Proof: </b> Note that using the method of finite differences, once we get to a constant term, the rest of the terms in the polynomial that have not been eliminated are going to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.  \nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/3/123c1a33e27ee965871b4460a59ec943f7ad18b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, a_2+1, a_3+8, a_4+27, a_5+64, a_6+125$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"335\" height=\"16\" /> is an arithmetic sequence, difference(let this be h)<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/2/4e2ad926cd8bc4f9d1579000bd52addf91947991.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=a_2-a_1+1=a_3-a_2+7=a_4-a_3+19=a_5-a_4+37=a_6-a_5+61$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"580\" height=\"15\" />, we get in general <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/7/7d7adc6587a87b806c0d55378fc84b3243300803.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i=0}^{n+1}f(i)-\\sum_{i=0}^{n}f(i)=a_{n+1}-a_n=f(n+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"332\" height=\"50\" />.  Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/effb88414967dcfb5b2e65b850ad2c3995bd8c31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2)+1=f(3)+7=f(4)+19=f(5)+37=f(6)+61$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"450\" height=\"18\" />.  We now have equations with our polynomials.  Subtract all consecutive equations to give us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/c/9ecab8092681b9ab172a3bed5af7ae500ddd6ed9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(3)-f(2)=-6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"137\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/e/e5e42c29e11d202153f2ec8d57cf91e2b7599937.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(4)-f(3)=-12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"146\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/f/37f7d34b4561f2bbab886e6e487fde18bf880ec1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(5)-f(4)=-18, f(6)-f(5)=-24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"301\" height=\"18\" />.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/8/8e845a915ef4eb43eaae12efed9009ff71e068d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=b_n*x^n+b_{n-1}*x^{n-1}+b_{n-2}*x^{n-2}+\\cdots b_2*x^2+b_1*x+b_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"530\" height=\"19\" />.  Note that subtracting two equations eliminates <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/5/ee5c7c921b3334f6ecf58c241eeea42acf0ce71e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" />, and we are going to be taking two more differences to get the equations equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.  These two more differences subtract the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/f/69fc4b9ed6d75d026557e7b06c2ed483c6ed0eda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"17\" /> term and the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/b/93b7aa611365e135f58aa09d52043ecd34855fe4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"17\" /> term, because by method of finite differences, you only have to take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> differences respectively to eliminate the linear/quadratic term.  Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is quadratic.   <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Now, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/a/2da39b9fea20557570c7efc90e056a207ae19584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=b_2x^2+b_1x+b_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"177\" height=\"19\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abb88988bde58a51f19f59c763ee7e64b140e96d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/3/93392873ade0e8887b8d04e8e9d8ac6438c7af4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i=0}^{0}f(0)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"95\" height=\"50\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/b/18b6b523413e7da3eea99cc80491857890718238.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_0=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"48\" height=\"15\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/3/5439423a07434e0049bc76b9649e8bf9e92d16b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2)+1=f(3)+7=f(4)+19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"253\" height=\"18\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/d/0dd37d464dedd2beedcffe93cef9d5773eeff36e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4b_2+2b_1+1=9b_2+3b_1+7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"228\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/4/06447a3858b0bb416dc93d6d200eac526c02ddf7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9b_2+3b_1+7=16b_2+4b_1+19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"246\" height=\"15\" />.  Subtract the LHS from the RHS of the equations to give us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/a/12a220128d23cc95f86af6aee939a9b5c7a50fec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5b_2+b_1+6=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"126\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/2/7225bcbab150c610d1229d91fd3b5a49e8b28318.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7b_2+b_1+12=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"135\" height=\"15\" />.  Subtract these two equations to give us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/c/fac59595bfef4ead8250db91e89c7003611155ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2b_2+6=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"88\" height=\"15\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/2/1f24be620f8b4cd0b8ed6bba18a2c554d8c0839f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_2=-3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"62\" height=\"15\" />.  Now, substitute this into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/a/12a220128d23cc95f86af6aee939a9b5c7a50fec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5b_2+b_1+6=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"126\" height=\"15\" /> to give us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/0/8e024e2943bdb66e8094cbac79e819c473e07482.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-15+6+b_1=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"134\" height=\"15\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/c/c8c602d6226abcaff23fdd8655ab090635670eee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1=9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"48\" height=\"15\" />.  Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/e/d2edbd8af7ecc61ad521f8d5dd88c085bb62d03f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=-3x^2+9x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"142\" height=\"19\" />.  \n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/1/191d57d1e5f185fb30c1bc518df495e0b7d7bbf2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)&lt;-2012$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"109\" height=\"18\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/1/5f17d4ba261471c887f24ecf02aacdbe03564615.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-3x^2+9x+2012&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"174\" height=\"16\" />, we are going to have this being true for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/a/d8a83e34b110659145e8703eaac970ae8011bf68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&gt; \\frac{-9\\pm \\sqrt{9^2-4(-3)(2012)}}{-6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"236\" height=\"41\" />.  Since we want <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> being positive, we use <span style=\"color:red\">$\\negative$ (Error compiling LaTeX. Unknown error_msg)</span> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/2/91205e81c98c486418902c88d5c396f5355491f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pm$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> to give us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/e/f2e725ad76acd010575994c8bd06a499889ac505.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&gt;\\frac{-9-\\sqrt{24225}}{-6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"143\" height=\"41\" />.  The RHS is the same as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/b/54b267e5de5b8b8ff5f26b6cc966a3c8e558cebb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{9+\\sqrt{24225}}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"94\" height=\"41\" />.  Our goal now is to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/a/c0a901ca2563c5bd149d675376847ee0a6334656.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{24225}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" /> approximately.  Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/4/f24df70a6ab0cee29ff11379aa53887f42375dfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$155^2=\\underline{15*16},2,5=24025$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"215\" height=\"18\" /> (where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/4/6e4a92593d1e8a04be9eda3fe5a44e662ae7439a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15*16, 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"70\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/4/7147c4f452069957d603daf7db67e27afcbd083f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$155^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"15\" />), therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/b/3ab5ceac9e87115d733223431ac3d066812707bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$156&gt;\\sqrt{24225}&gt;155$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"163\" height=\"18\" />, and substitute this into our equation for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> to give a smallest possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> being <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/b/77b0f94a3f779be40d62788501cea447419beba0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{156+9}{6}&gt;x&gt;\\frac{155+9}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"182\" height=\"37\" /> to give us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/a/2aa7b3f70f770281c754cd2c34d449a7f79642f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$27.5&gt;x&gt;27.\\overline{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"123\" height=\"15\" /> and hence the smallest possible positive integer value for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/b/a7b7ae7da01575cdec96fc6750f80a12b9e0091b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{028}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"40\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_II_2012_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Another way of finding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is noticing that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/1/83194be4f311201f3e8f36071c605bf0a4be6008.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n-a_{n-1}=\\sum_{i=0}^{n}f(i)-\\sum_{i=0}^{n-1}f(i)= f(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"301\" height=\"50\" /> and that the terms of the arithmetic sequence are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/2/422f8a0cf494987dc221cccdc1bd50e94a238859.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n+(n-1)^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"103\" height=\"19\" />. The difference of arithmetic sequences are constant, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/4/e84a025de74793cc149fb955f4daf0dd897f5441.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n+(n-1)^3-(a_{n-1}+(n-2)^3)= f(n) + 3n^2 - 9n + 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"446\" height=\"19\" /> is constant. Let that constant be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/3/783df88a8820385e2f5f8bf24cd32b7ed5652318.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)+3n^2-9n+7 =c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"191\" height=\"19\" /> and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/a/b0a1d0dde8ff505af91514f643afdb79edf192a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n) = -3n^2+9n -7+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"205\" height=\"19\" />. The solution follows as above.\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018040702\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.030 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.587 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 329/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 12450/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:10987:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018040702 and revision id 68589. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}